From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:51:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: drop the PMU RTC alias

t8132-jxxx.dtsi now gives the M4 boards a PMU RTC on the nub SPMI bus
and names it rtc1. The J604 replaces that bus with its own and keeps
the SMC RTC as its clock, so the alias points at nothing and the DTB
does not build. Drop it on the J604.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index 514d38afe5..095ef1ccc2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -33,6 +33,16 @@
 /delete-node/ &{/soc/mbox@0};
 /delete-node/ &{/soc/spmi@0};
 
+/*
+ * The shared PMU RTC (rtc1 = &pmu_rtc) sits on the SPMI bus deleted above; the J604's
+ * clock is the SMC RTC (rtc0), so the alias has no target here.
+ */
+/ {
+	aliases {
+		/delete-property/ rtc1;
+	};
+};
+
 /* The speaker amps and the sound card, gated as on 1.617 (macaudio + tas2764 safety chain). */
 &{/soc/i2c@3ad01c000/codec@38} { status = "okay"; };
 &{/soc/i2c@3ad01c000/codec@39} { status = "okay"; };
-- 
2.43.0

